{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"087d679e636e08063ee24ae523a193d831c5eb83530e7e4d4788bba6748c3e31","digest":{"component_or_area":"Reconciler JQL fetcher","key_entities":["fetcher.py","jql_active","jql_done_recent","statusCategory","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_multi_project.py","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_paging_split.py","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_once.py"],"problem_keywords":["reconciler","jira","status category","active set","done status","workflow","jql","client workflow"],"propositions":["The reconciler hardcodes status != \"Done\" for active-set queries, which misses custom closed-equivalent statuses (Closed, Resolved, Cancelled) used by client workflows.","Issues in non-Done statusCategory statuses are incorrectly pulled into the active working set and treated as active, causing spurious outbound mutations.","jql_done_recent misses issues in custom Done-category statuses, leaving them out of the recent-Done snapshot.","Switching from literal status = \"Done\" to statusCategory = \"Done\" / statusCategory != \"Done\" makes the active/done scoping workflow-agnostic and correct for all Jira workflows.","The fix requires updating JQL builders in fetcher.py and adding test coverage verifying statusCategory predicates for single and multi-project fan-out."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787401265233343001,"uuid":"7d535e01-b54d-46ab-aed0-f6968d62407d"}